<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer says confident of right ECB appointments.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says confident of right ECB appointments.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Tuesday he was confident the right appointments would be made to the future European Central Bank after initial members are chosen for the new European currency.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer, speaking in English at the Global 24 conference in Frankfurt, also reaffirmed his support for new European Monetary Institute President Wim Duisenberg to be on the new central bank board.</p>
<p>&quot;...I am confident that (we) will make a right decision. And a right decision means -- he is sitting on the right of me,&quot; Tietmeyer said, referring to Duisenberg sitting next to him on the panel.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
